From: macos-local research
Subject: [PATCH] Per-vCPU PAuth VA parameter cache and SSSE3 QARMA5/QARMA3

Cache aa64_pauth_va_parameters() per (mmu_idx, TCR) on realized CPUs and
accelerate architected QARMA5/QARMA3 on x86_64 SSSE3 hosts via 16-nibble
pshufb S-boxes and permutations, self-tested across 2,048 deterministic
random vectors at CPU realize.

diff --git a/target/arm/cpu.c b/target/arm/cpu.c
--- a/target/arm/cpu.c
+++ b/target/arm/cpu.c
@@ -2773,6 +2773,10 @@
         if (cpu_isar_feature(aa64_mte, cpu)) {
             assert(dcz_blocklen >= 2 * TAG_GRANULE);
         }
+#ifdef CONFIG_TCG
+        arm_pauth_qarma_selftest();
+#endif
+        env->pauth_va_cache_enabled = true;
     }
 
     qemu_init_vcpu(cs);
